# Title: Potential File Extension Spoofing Using Right-to-Left Override
# ID: 979baf41-ca44-4540-9d0c-4fcef3b5a3a4
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Jonathan Peters (Nextron Systems), Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2024-11-17
# Tags: attack.execution, attack.stealth, attack.t1036.002
# Description: Detects suspicious filenames that contain a right-to-left override character and a potentially spoofed file extensions.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((file.path:*3pm.* OR file.path:*4pm.* OR file.path:*cod.* OR file.path:*fdp.* OR file.path:*ftr.* OR file.path:*gepj.* OR file.path:*gnp.* OR file.path:*gpj.* OR file.path:*ism.* OR file.path:*lmth.* OR file.path:*nls.* OR file.path:*piz.* OR file.path:*slx.* OR file.path:*tdo.* OR file.path:*vsc.* OR file.path:*vwm.* OR file.path:*xcod.* OR file.path:*xslx.* OR file.path:*xtpp.*)) AND ((file.path:*\\u202e* OR file.path:*[U+202E]* OR file.path:*‮*)))
